  "summary": "PostgreSQL pg_dump heap buffer overflow executes arbitrary code",
  "details": "Heap buffer overflow in PostgreSQL pg_dump of long function transform lists allows an object creator to execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running pg_dump, via a crafted transform list.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.6, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.",
